# WS6-02 / WS5-11 (float formatting and host/Amiga parity). Sources: spec/decisions.md
# S2a and spec/04-expressions.md §12 (template float placeholders use six significant
# digits — the C99 %g default precision, C99 7.19.6.1); spec/02 §2 (f64 is IEEE double);
# spec/17 §11 (determinism) and the corpus rule that one program prints the same text on
# every profile. NaN and infinity spellings are not specified; the expectation uses the
# C99 %g spellings, and a divergence between profiles is the finding either way.
# Expected: the two lines below on host, hosted-amiga, and hosted-amiga-13.
profiles: host hosted-amiga hosted-amiga-13
expect: output
contrast: let b: f64 = 2.5; ==> let b: f64 = 3.5;
contrast-expect: output
--- output
0.1 2.5 1.23457e+08 1e+300 -0
nan inf -inf
--- contrast-output
0.1 3.5 1.23457e+08 1e+300 -0
nan inf -inf
